"hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1696,"**
Narrated to us Naṣr ibn ʿAlī al-Jahḍamī, he informed us Nuʿaym — meaning Ibn Qays al-Ḥudānī —, he narrated to us ʿAmr ibn Mālik, from Abū al-Jawzāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās (RA), who said:
“A beautiful woman, one of the most beautiful of people, used to pray behind the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ). Some of the people would advance to the first row so as not to see her, while others would hang back until they were in the last row. When he bowed, he would glance from beneath his armpit. So Allāh, the Exalted and Majestic, revealed regarding her case:
‘And We already know the predecessors among you, and We already know the successors [to come].’”
[Sūrah al-Ḥijr, 15:24]"
1697,"Narrated to us Abu Musa, who said: Narrated to us Nuḥ ibn Qays al-Ḥudāniyy, who mentioned the hadith with this meaning.

Narrated to us al-Faḍl ibn Yaʿqūb, who said: Narrated to us Nuḥ, on the authority of ʿAmr ibn Mālik, with something similar to it.

**CHAPTER:**"
